Near misses for builder_directive_outside_datasource in a .ssl script: a
variable whose name contains a directive word (`sDsn`), directive text in
a string literal and a comment, and an object property named like one
(`oCfg:TableName`). None is a directive keyword.
-- input.ssl --
/* reads :DSN and :TABLENAME settings from the config table;
:DECLARE sDsn, sNote, oCfg;
sDsn := "DATABASE";
sNote := ":NULLASBLANK := true;";
oCfg := CreateUdObject();
oCfg:TableName := "stockList";
:RETURN sDsn + sNote + oCfg:TableName;
-- format --
